      "preview": "אָוָה: tradução portuguesa integral; 43 remissões preservadas.",
      "html": "† I. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אָוָה</span>]</big>  <strong>verbo: inclinar-se, desejar (</strong>cf. radical <strong>2)</strong>.<br><strong>Piel</strong>  perfeito <span dir=\"rtl\">אִוָּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 132:13\" href=\"/Psalms.132.13\">ψ 132:13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אִוְּתָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:1\" href=\"/Micah.7.1\">Mi 7:1</a> + etc.; imperfeito, 3ª pessoa fem. sing. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּאַוֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.20\">Dt 12:20</a> + 4 ocorrências—<em>desejar</em>; o sujeito geralmente é <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶפֶשׁ</span>; o objeto, frutos <a data-ref=\"Micah 7:1\" href=\"/Micah.7.1\">Mi 7:1</a> (em sentido metafórico); carne (para comer) <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 2:16\" href=\"/I_Samuel.2.16\">1 S 2:16</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.20\">Dt 12:20</a> (seguido de infinitivo <span dir=\"rtl\">לֶאֱכֹל בָּשָׂר</span>); comida e bebida <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:26\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.26\">Dt 14:26</a>; acerca de rei que deseja governar, <span dir=\"rtl\">וּמָלַכְתָּ בְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר־תְּאַוֶּה נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 3:21\" href=\"/II_Samuel.3.21\">2 S 3:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 11:37\" href=\"/I_Kings.11.37\">1 K 11:37</a>; objeto: <em>o mal</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">(רַע)</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 21:10\" href=\"/Proverbs.21.10\">Pr 21:10</a>; numa ocorrência, o objeto é <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 26:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.26.9\">Is 26:9</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">נַפְשִׁי אִוִּיתִךָ בַּלַּיְלָה</span>; acerca de Deus <span dir=\"rtl\">וְנַפְשׁוֹ אִוְּתָה וַיַּעַשׂ</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 23:13\" href=\"/Job.23.13\">Jb 23:13</a>; desejando Sião como morada (passagens tardias, os únicos casos sem <span dir=\"rtl\">נפשׁ</span>) <a data-ref=\"Psalms 132:13\" href=\"/Psalms.132.13\">ψ 132:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Psalms 132:14\" href=\"/Psalms.132.14\">14</a>;<br><strong>Hitpael</strong>  perfeito <span dir=\"rtl\">הִתְאַוָּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 21:26\" href=\"/Proverbs.21.26\">Pr 21:26</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הִתְאַוֵּיתִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 17:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.17.16\">Je 17:16</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הִתְאַוּוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:4\" href=\"/Numbers.11.4\">Nu 11:4</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">וְהִתְאַוִּיתֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 34:10\" href=\"/Numbers.34.10\">Nu 34:10</a>; imperfeito <span dir=\"rtl\">יִתְאַוֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 6:2\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.6.2\">Ec 6:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיִּתְאַוֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:15\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.15\">2 S 23:15</a>; forma apocopada <span dir=\"rtl\">וְיִתְאַו</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 45:12\" href=\"/Psalms.45.12\">ψ 45:12</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיִּתְאַו</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:17\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.17\">1 Ch 11:17</a> etc.—particípio fem. sing. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְאַוָּה</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 13:4\" href=\"/Proverbs.13.4\">Pr 13:4</a>; masc. plural <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְאַוִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 5:18\" href=\"/Amos.5.18\">Am 5:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:34\" href=\"/Numbers.11.34\">Nu 11:34</a>—<em>desejar, ansiar por, cobiçar</em>, acerca dos apetites corporais; por alimentos delicados <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:4\" href=\"/Numbers.11.4\">Nu 11:4</a> (E; seguido de acusativo cognato) = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 106:14\" href=\"/Psalms.106.14\">ψ 106:14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:34\" href=\"/Numbers.11.34\">Nu 11:34</a> (E); seguido de ל <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.3\">Pr 23:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 23:6\" href=\"/Proverbs.23.6\">6</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 6:2\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.6.2\">Ec 6:2</a> (seguido de acusativo); ver também <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 13:4\" href=\"/Proverbs.13.4\">Pr 13:4</a> (uso absoluto, com o sujeito <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶפֶשׁ</span>); uso absoluto acerca de sede extrema <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:15\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.15\">2 S 23:15</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:17\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.17\">1 Ch 11:17</a>; acerca do rei que deseja a beleza <span dir=\"rtl\">(יֳפִי)</span> da princesa <a data-ref=\"Psalms 45:12\" href=\"/Psalms.45.12\">ψ 45:12</a> (seguido de acusativo); do homem cobiçoso <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 21:26\" href=\"/Proverbs.21.26\">Pr 21:26</a> (seguido de acusativo cognato); objeto: <span dir=\"rtl\">בֵּית רֵעֲךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 5:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.5.17\">Dt 5:18</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">חמד</span>); seguido de infinitivo <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 24:1\" href=\"/Proverbs.24.1\">Pr 24:1</a> (referindo-se ao desejo de má companhia); objeto: <span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹם י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 5:18\" href=\"/Amos.5.18\">Am 5:18</a> (acusativo; acerca de anseio presunçoso e temerário); cf. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 17:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.17.16\">Je 17:16</a>. (<a data-ref=\"Numbers 34:7\" href=\"/Numbers.34.7\">Nu 34:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 34:8\" href=\"/Numbers.34.8\">8</a> em lugar de <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּתָאוּ</span>—Piel de <span dir=\"rtl\">תאה</span>—Di propõe <span dir=\"rtl\">תִּתְאַוֻּ</span> e indaga se esta forma e <span dir=\"rtl\">הִתְאַוִּיתֶם</span> no versículo <a data-ref=\"Numbers 34:10\" href=\"/Numbers.34.10\">10</a> não provêm de <span dir=\"rtl\">אוה</span>, = <em>desejar para vós mesmos</em>.)",
