      "preview": "אוּפָז: tradução portuguesa integral; 14 referências documentais preservadas.",
      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אוּפָז</span></big>  <strong>(nome próprio de lugar</strong> desconhecido e duvidoso<strong>)</strong> de onde procedia ouro, <span dir=\"rtl\">זָהָב מֵא׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.9\">Je 10:9</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כֶּֽתֶם א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:5\" href=\"/Daniel.10.5\">Dn 10:5</a>; assim Thes <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:18\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.18\">1 K 10:18</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">זָהָב מוּפָז</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\">מוּפָז</span> = <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵא׳</span>); mas 𝔊 traz δόκιμος, e <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.17\">2 Ch 9:17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">טָהוֹר</span>; daí MV e Klo entendem <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּפָז</span> como particípio hofal de <span dir=\"rtl\">פזז</span>; ver esse verbete. Klo lê <span dir=\"rtl\">אוֹפִיר</span> (ver esse verbete) em lugar de <span dir=\"rtl\">אוּפָז</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.9\">Je 10:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:5\" href=\"/Daniel.10.5\">Dn 10:5</a>; considerando <span dir=\"rtl\">כֶּתֶם אוֹפִיר</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:12\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.12\">Is 13:12</a> corrompido; ver Siegf<sup>ThLZ, 7 nov. 1883, 530</sup>; ele explica <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵא׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.9\">Je 10:9</a> como erro por <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּפָז</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:18\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.18\">1 K 10:18</a>; e <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:5\" href=\"/Daniel.10.5\">Dn 10:5</a> como tomado de <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.9\">Je 10:9</a>; em <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.9\">Je 10:9</a> Gie lê <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵאוֹפִיר</span>; Du propõe esta leitura ou <span dir=\"rtl\">מוּפָז</span> (ver <a data-ref=\"BDB, פָּזַז\" href=\"/BDB,_פָּזַז\", dir=\"rtl\">פזז</a>); ler <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵאוֹפִיר</span> talvez também em <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:5\" href=\"/Daniel.10.5\">Dn 10:5</a> (Dr).",
